  "title": "UserIcon Impact in Patient Chart",
  "updatedAt": 1793523188882,
  "answers": [
    {
      "id": "tzxJ8yQxbS4g2uYw",
      "productId": "openmrs",
      "question": "If `UserIcon` in the OpenMRS frontend framework (openmrs-esm-core) changed its behaviour, which code in the patient chart app (openmrs-esm-patient-chart) uses it and could be affected?",
      "generation": "g-b59a21",
      "kind": "partial",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "`UserIcon` is defined in the framework at [1]. It is a `memo`-wrapped `forwardRef` component that forwards its props to the generic `Icon` component with the sprite id `omrs-icon-user` [2]. Note that the accepted props are narrow — only `className`, `fill` and `size` [3] — and `Icon` clamps an invalid `size` to 20, logging an error [4].",
          "citations": [
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## Confirmed affected code in `openmrs-esm-patient-chart`",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Both real consumers use `UserIcon` inside a local `InfoTooltip` showing the orderer of a medication:",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- **Orders app — medication record.** `medication-record.component.tsx` imports it [5] and renders it as the toggle button of a Carbon `Toggletip` with `size={16}` [6]. The tooltip is rendered by `MedicationRecord` with the orderer display name [7].\n- **Medications app — medication details table.** `medications-details-table.component.tsx` imports it [8] and renders it with `size={16}` inside the same-named local `InfoTooltip`, which is itself wrapped in an `IconButton` [9]. That tooltip is used only as the `startDate` cell content, and only when not printing [10].",
          "citations": [
            5,
            6,
            7,
            8,
            9,
            10
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because both call sites pass only `size={16}`, the parts of `UserIcon`/`Icon` behaviour they actually depend on are: the icon rendering itself (sprite id, SVG sizing, `omrs-icon` class) and the size-to-pixel mapping. A change to `forwardRef`/ref handling, default fill, or the size handling (e.g. the `<= 0 || > 72` clamp) would show up in these two places; anything that changes the accepted props would break their `size` prop at type-check time.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## Test coverage",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "No test in the patient-chart app mocks or asserts on `UserIcon` (searching the repo finds no `UserIcon` outside these two files, and no `omrs-icon-user` string), so the change would only be caught indirectly:",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- `MedicationRecord` is rendered for real in `medication-record.test.tsx`, but those tests only stub `useDrugOrderByUuid` [11] — the real framework import path is used, so the icon must render without throwing, but nothing asserts its output.\n- `medications-details-table.test.tsx` also renders the real component and mocks `@openmrs/esm-patient-common-lib` only [12].\n- The orders-app table test replaces `MedicationRecord` with a mock packages/esm-patient-orders-app/src/components/order-details-table.test.tsx, so that path is insulated.",
          "citations": [
            11,
            12
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## Name clashes (not affected)",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "An `InfoTooltip` also exists in `packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/overview/common-overview.component.tsx`, but it is an unrelated local component rendering an `Information` icon, not `UserIcon` packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/overview/common-overview.component.tsx. The framework's own `UserIcon` stubs in `mock.tsx` and `mock-jest.tsx` are separate declarations.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## Could not verify",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- I only searched this one repository; other apps in scope (dispensing, stock management, admin tools, etc.) may consume `UserIcon` too.\n- Ref forwarding is untested here: no patient-chart call site passes a `ref` to `UserIcon`, so a ref-handling change would not surface in these files.",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
